 "drug_rule": "Finasteride (5 mg) reduces prostate size by inhibiting 5-alpha-reductase, but it also has mild vasodilatory effects. Terazosin, a first-line alpha-blocker for BPH, directly antagonizes alpha-1 receptors on vascular smooth muscle and the prostate. The combination produces additive hypotensive effects, increasing the risk of symptomatic hypotension, syncope, and falls. This interaction is well-documented and contraindicated in many guidelines.",
